# Sternhalma, the external port (examples/sternhalma), played by drag and
# drop on the page driver (tests/corpus/README.md, the `browser/` kind).
# It is a corpus case held out of the gates: the case costs ~5 000 million
# instructions against the 4 300 million budget, and a load alone is over
# it (PORTING.md, *The play script*). Replay it with
#
#     beni build --out=out src
#     node ../../tests/browser/driver.mjs \
#         --dom=../../tests/browser/happy-dom.mjs out/_main.mjs \
#         play/sternhalma.steps | diff - play/sternhalma.expected
#
# The board is 121 cells drawn row by row, sorted by z then x, so a cell is
# the n-th child of the board's div: 8 is (2,-5) in red's home, 17 is
# (2,-4), 10 is (4,-5), 30 is (2,-3), 61 is the centre (0,0), 115 is (-1,5)
# in purple's home and 106 is (-1,4). A drag is the bubbling events a
# browser fires: dragstart on the piece, then dragover and drop on the cell
# under it, whose handlers allow the drop by preventing the default, as
# Elm's `preventDefaultOn` does; dragend on the piece when no drop took it.
#
# Two players: red starts in the top triangle, purple in the bottom one.
click .items-center>button:nth-child(1)
# It is red's turn, so purple's piece does not start a drag.
drag div[style*=width]>div:nth-child(115)>div dragstart
# Red picks up (2,-5): the two cells it may reach are ringed.
drag div[style*=width]>div:nth-child(8)>div dragstart
drag div[style*=width]>div:nth-child(17)>div dragover
# A step to (2,-4); purple's turn.
drag div[style*=width]>div:nth-child(17)>div drop
# Purple drops on the centre, out of reach: nothing moves, the rings go,
# and it is still purple's turn.
drag div[style*=width]>div:nth-child(115)>div dragstart
drag div[style*=width]>div:nth-child(61)>div drop
# A drag let go off the board ends with dragend alone: the rings go.
drag div[style*=width]>div:nth-child(115)>div dragstart
drag div[style*=width]>div:nth-child(115)>div dragend
# A step to (-1,4).
drag div[style*=width]>div:nth-child(115)>div dragstart
drag div[style*=width]>div:nth-child(106)>div drop
# Red's multi-jump: (4,-5) is ringed to its two steps, to (2,-5) by one
# hop over (3,-5), and to (2,-3) by a second hop over (2,-4), which no
# single hop reaches. It lands there.
drag div[style*=width]>div:nth-child(10)>div dragstart
drag div[style*=width]>div:nth-child(30)>div drop
# New Game goes back to choosing the number of players.
click button.bg-gray-200
